      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1643542290,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I got this:\n```\n$ appstream-util validate resources/freedesktop/org.wireshark.Wireshark.metainfo.xml\nresources/freedesktop/org.wireshark.Wireshark.metainfo.xml: FAILED:\n• tag-invalid           : Expected children for tag\n• attribute-invalid     : <screenshot> width too large [https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsug_html/images/ws-stats-conversations.png] maximum is 1600px\n• attribute-invalid     : <screenshot> height too large [https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsug_html/images/ws-stats-conversations.png] maximum is 900px\n• style-invalid         : <image> has vertical padding [https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsug_html/images/ws-stats-conversations.png]\n• style-invalid         : <image> has horizontal padding [https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsug_html/images/ws-stats-conversations.png]\n• tag-missing           : <release> required\nValidation of files failed\n```\nThe `tag-invalid` and `tag-missing` issues go away after running `tools/update-appdata.py`, the image issues can't be fixed in the file. It is safe to proceed.",
